  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「マンリョウ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%9E%E3%83%B3%E3%83%AA%E3%83%A7%E3%82%A6",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 108680219,
      "text": "マンリョウ は、サクラソウ科ヤブコウジ属の常緑小低木。林内に生育し、冬に熟す果実が美しいので栽培され、特に名前がめでたいのでセンリョウ科のセンリョウ（千両）などとともに正月の縁起物とされる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Ardisia crenata」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ardisia_crenata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1332441931,
      "text": "Ardisia crenata is a species of flowering plant in the primrose family, Primulaceae, that is native to East Asia. It is known by a variety of names such as Christmas berry, coral ardisia, coral bush, coralberry, coralberry tree, hen's-eyes, and spiceberry. A. crenata is a compact shrub that reaches 1 metre (3.3 ft), often with a single stem. Leaves are dark green, thick, glossy, and have tightly waved edges. The flowers are small, white or reddish, fragrant, and form clusters. The fruit is a glossy, bright red drupe. The seeds are able to germinate under a dense canopy and are dispersed by birds and humans."
    }
  },
